{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786730582,"nonce":"qQf9UAit3MI/ovtcXUDwxoLzh9Q=","title":"`QueueReconcile`'s two workers cap the source fan-out at ~30 tenants, and the number is a binding SPEC row with no config knob","was":"**What is wrong.** `QueueReconcile` runs two workers — `internal/platform/jobs/client.go:36`, `QueueReconcile: 2` — and every job the reconcile fan-out enqueues lands on it, at the same kind and priority as the per-source passes that dial a customer's Alertmanager or Prometheus. Those passes are network-bound and may hold a worker for the full sixty seconds `source.reconcile` is registered with (`internal/platform/jobs/registry.go:211`, `Timeout: 60 * time.Second`), against a tick that repeats every thirty (`internal/app/workers.go`, `reconcileFanOutInterval`). Two slow upstreams are therefore enough to stall both remaining slots, and the tenant walk queues behind the same two workers as the work it schedules."}]}